Set `self.high` first. Until every field is set, only fields that are already set can be read.
diagnostics/operators.em:60:15: a subclass could override `compare`, so construction cannot call it through `self`
          print(self > Level(0))
                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
A subclass's version would run before that subclass has set its own fields. Move what it does into a private method, such as `_compare`, and use that instead.
